# Task 149-007: Docker Worker Exit Pattern Final Fix

## Problem
Sprint 146 NO_GO + Sprint 148 TD: Container SIGKILL before .result write. OOM path + partial write still open.

## Current State Analysis
1. Container-side EXIT trap exists (on_exit) — handles git diff partial work detection
2. Host-side monitor (monitorContainer) writes fallback .result when container exits without one
3. kill() uses docker stop --time=15 then docker kill (SIGKILL, not SIGTERM)

## Changes Required

### 1. spawn-backend-docker.ts — kill() method improvement
- Change fallback `docker kill` to use `--signal=SIGTERM` instead of bare SIGKILL
- Add result polling after stop (up to 20s wait for .result write)

### 2. spawn-backend-docker.ts — monitorContainer fallback improvements
- Add signal_info to fallback notes (exit > 128 → signal number)
- Add tokenUsage to fallback result JSON (required since Sprint 140)
- Add partial write detection: if .result exists but JSON parse fails → overwrite with NO_GO

### 3. spawn-backend-docker.ts — shell script EXIT trap improvements
- Add signal_info to container-side fallback JSON
- Add tokenUsage to container-side fallback JSON
- Keep SIGTERM trap separate for fsync path

### 4. tests/backends/docker-exit-final.test.ts — 6 new tests
- SIGKILL → result file written with NO_GO + exitCode + signal_info
- Normal completion → cleanup_result no-op
- SIGTERM graceful → result written normally
- OOM kill (exit 137) → result written with signal_info
- Partial write scenario → detected and NO_GO result
- Docker stop --time=15 → grace period honored (kill method test)

## Files Modified
- src/orchestra/spawn-backend-docker.ts (kill + monitorContainer + shell script)
- tests/backends/docker-exit-final.test.ts (NEW — 6 tests)
